## Windows / PowerShell — DO NOT REPEAT THESE FAILURES

| Mistake | What happened | Correct approach |
|--------|----------------|------------------|
| `cmd1 && cmd2` | `InvalidEndOfLine` — `&&` is not a statement separator in **Windows PowerShell 5.x** | Chain with `;` on one line, or run **separate** Shell tool calls |
| `curl -s ...` | PowerShell aliases `curl` → `Invoke-WebRequest` (wrong params) | Always use **`curl.exe`** for GitHub API / HTTP |
| `gh issue list` | `gh` not in PATH on this machine | Install GitHub CLI, or use **`curl.exe`** + REST API; for auth use `$env:GITHUB_TOKEN` |
| `winget list` without need | Command hung ~47s, interrupted | Avoid slow discovery commands; check known paths first |
| Assuming `gh` works | Silent failure blocked issue triage | Probe first: `Get-Command gh -EA SilentlyContinue` or test `curl.exe` |

### Safe command templates (copy these patterns)

```powershell
# Change directory + one action
Set-Location "c:\Users\shiva\OneDrive\Desktop\propops"; git status

# GitHub API (public read)
curl.exe -s -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" "https://api.github.com/repos/lnsolspvtltd/propops/issues?state=open&per_page=20"

# GitHub API (authenticated — PR create, merge, comments)
$headers = @{ Authorization = "Bearer $env:GITHUB_TOKEN"; Accept = "application/vnd.github+json" }
# Use curl.exe -H "Authorization: Bearer $env:GITHUB_TOKEN" ...

# GitHub CLI when installed
& "C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe" pr list --repo lnsolspvtltd/propops
```

**Never** use bash-only heredocs (`<<'EOF'`) in PowerShell commits; use a here-string or `-m "message"` for git commit.

## GitHub issue cycle (one issue at a time)

Process **oldest open issue first** unless labels/dependencies say otherwise. Do not start the next issue until the current PR is **merged** (or user says stop).

1. **Discover** — List open issues (`curl.exe` or `gh`). Read full body + acceptance criteria.
2. **Branch** — Checkout existing issue branch from `origin` or create: `phase3/issue-{number}` (match repo convention).
3. **Implement** — Minimal diff; match existing FastAPI/Next.js patterns; run tests before push.
4. **Push** — `git push -u origin HEAD` on the issue branch only (not force-push `main`).
5. **PR** — Open PR to `main`; body includes Summary + Test plan; link `Closes #N`.
6. **Invoke FORGE** — Request code review (see **FORGE review invocation** below). Do not wait passively.
7. **Review loop (max 3 iterations)** — Poll until FORGE finishes → implement all feedback → push → re-invoke. Track **1/3, 2/3, 3/3**.
8. **Merge gate** — See **NEVER merge without FORGE approval** below. Only merge after explicit APPROVED review.
9. **Escalation** — After **3 iterations** without FORGE approval: **STOP**, post summary on PR, ask **external user** for decision. Do **not** merge.
10. **Next** — Return to step 1 for the next open issue only after merge + issue closed.

## NEVER merge without FORGE approval (mandatory — no exceptions)

**Do not merge a PR unless ONE of these is true:**

1. **FORGE (or Claude code-review bot) has submitted a GitHub review with state `APPROVED`**, or
2. An **external human user** (founder/client — not the agent) explicitly says “merge PR #N” in chat.

**If neither condition is met, you MUST stop and wait.** Polling for reviews is required; merging early is forbidden.

### What counts as approval

| Signal | Merge? |
|--------|--------|
| `reviewDecision: APPROVED` / FORGE review `state: APPROVED` | Yes — after CI passes |
| `reviewDecision: CHANGES_REQUESTED` | No — fix feedback, push, re-poll |
| Empty reviews / no `reviewDecision` yet | **No — wait for FORGE** |
| Agent thinks code is fine | **No** |
| Checks green but no review | **No** |
| User says “continue the issue cycle” | **No** — that is not merge permission |
| External user: “merge PR #43” | Yes (if CI passes) |

### Forbidden commands until approved

- `gh pr merge` (any variant)
- GitHub API `PUT .../pulls/{n}/merge`
- Any other merge path (squash, rebase, admin merge)

**Past mistake:** PR **#42** (issue #35) was merged without FORGE approval. Do **not** repeat.

## FORGE review invocation (required after PR open/update)

After opening or pushing to a PR, **actively invoke FORGE** — do not assume a webhook will fire.

### Primary method (Helix `review_pr`)

From `ln-sols-multi-agent` (requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` + `GITHUB_TOKEN` in `.env`):

```powershell
Set-Location "c:\Users\shiva\OneDrive\Desktop\LN SOLS MULTI AGENT\ln-sols-multi-agent"
python -c "from agents.forge.tools.code_reviewer import review_pr; r = review_pr('https://github.com/lnsolspvtltd/propops/pull/N'); print(r.review.overall_rating, r.review.approved)"
```

FORGE posts a GitHub PR review comment (`## 🔨 FORGE Code Review`) with rating and issues.

**Do NOT use** `run_review_loop` / `scripts/run_forge_reviews.py` for PropOps agent workflow — those auto-fix via ANVIL and may auto-merge. PropOps agent implements fixes locally.

### Alternative triggers

| Method | When to use |
|--------|-------------|
| PR comment `@forge review` | If overseer webhook is running on EC2 |
| `python scripts/run_forge_reviews.py --pr URL --max-iter 1` | One-shot review only (agent still fixes locally) |
| GitHub Actions `forge-review.yml` | Only on `ln-sols-multi-agent` repo, not PropOps |

### 3-iteration review cap (mandatory)

Each PR gets at most **3 complete cycles**:

1. **Invoke FORGE** → wait for review comment/review to appear
2. **Implement all feedback** on the issue branch → run tests → push
3. **Increment counter** (1/3, 2/3, 3/3) and repeat from step 1

**After iteration 3 without approval:**

- Post a PR comment: iteration count, remaining issues, merge blocked
- **STOP** — do not merge, do not start next issue
- Ask **external user** (founder) to approve merge or give direction

**Goal:** Fix everything FORGE asks within ≤3 rounds so approval happens before escalation.

### What counts as FORGE approval

| Signal | Merge? |
|--------|--------|
| GitHub `reviewDecision: APPROVED` | Yes — after CI passes |
| FORGE review body contains `✅ APPROVED` and `overall_rating: approved` with no critical/major issues | Yes — after CI passes |
| `CHANGES_REQUESTED` / `❌ CHANGES REQUIRED` / critical or major issues listed | No — fix and re-invoke (if iterations remain) |
| No FORGE review yet | No — invoke FORGE, then poll |
| 3 iterations exhausted, still not approved | No — escalate to external user |

### Review polling (after FORGE invoked)

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe" pr view 43 --repo lnsolspvtltd/propops --json reviewDecision,reviews,state
& "C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe" api repos/lnsolspvtltd/propops/pulls/43/comments
& "C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe" api repos/lnsolspvtltd/propops/issues/43/comments
```

If `CHANGES_REQUESTED` or inline comments exist: checkout issue branch → fix → test → push → reply → re-invoke FORGE → poll again (respect 3-iteration cap).

### Do not start the next issue until the current one is merged with approval

Example: do **not** implement #37 until PR for #36 is merged **with** FORGE approval.

### Local git cautions (observed on this machine)

- `origin/main` may contain **invalid Windows paths** (newline in filename) — `git checkout origin/main` fails. Branch from **local `main`** after path cleanup commits are applied.
- `main` may be **ahead of `origin/main`** with unpushed commits — push cleanup to `main` when user allows so remotes are Windows-safe.
- Do not use stale branch `phase3/issue-33-35` (large deletions vs current `main`).
- **Do not commit** unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Do not force-push** `main`.

